{
  "title": "92: Al-Lail الليل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "There are 21 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward of reciting this Surah is so much that the one who recites it will be pleased when he sees it in his Book of Deeds. His inspiration of good deeds (Tawfiq) will also increase.\nIf recited 15 times before sleeping, one will dream about what pleases him most. Reciting it in the Isha prayers carries the reward of completing a quarter of the Holy Qur’an and is guaranteed that the prayers are accepted.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(1)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAA.\nBy the Night as it conceals (the light); \nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا تَجَلّٰىۙ‏(2)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA TAJALLAA.\nBy the Day as it appears in glory; \nوَمَا خَلَقَ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰٓىۙ‏(3)\nWA MAA KHALAQAZ ZAKARA WAL UNSAA.\nBy (the mystery of) the creation of male and female;- \nاِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتّٰىؕ‏(4)\nINNA SA’YAKUM LA-SHATTAA.\nVerily, (the ends) ye strive for are diverse. \nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اَعْطٰى وَاتَّقٰىۙ‏(5)\nFA-AMMAA MAN A-A’TAA WAT TAQAA.\nSo he who gives (in charity) and fears (Allah), \nوَصَدَّقَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(6)\nWA SADDAQA BIL-HUSNAA.\nAnd (in all sincerity) testifies to the best, \nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْيُسْرٰىؕ‏(7)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-YUSRAA.\nWe will indeed make smooth for him the path to Bliss. \nوَاَمَّا مَنْۢ بَخِلَ وَاسْتَغْنٰىۙ‏(8)\nWA AMMAA MAM BAKHELA WAS TAGHNAA.\nBut he who is a greedy miser and thinks himself self-sufficient, \nوَكَذَّبَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(9)\nWA KAZZABA BIL-HUSNAA.\nAnd gives the lie to the best, \nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْعُسْرٰىؕ‏(10)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-U’SRAA.\nWe will indeed make smooth for him the path to Misery; \nوَمَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُ مَالُهٗۤ اِذَا تَرَدّٰىؕ‏(11)\nWA MAA YUGHNEE A’NHO MAALOHU EZAA TARADDAA.\nNor will his wealth profit him when he falls headlong (into the Pit). \nاِنَّ عَلَيْنَا لَلْهُدٰىۖ‏(12)\nINNA A’LAYNAA LAL-HODAA.\nVerily We take upon Ourselves to guide, \nوَاِنَّ لَنَا لَلْاٰخِرَةَ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(13)\nWA INNA LANAA LAL-AAKHERATA WAL OOLAA.\nAnd verily unto Us (belong) the End and the Beginning. \nفَاَنْذَرْتُكُمْ نَارًا تَلَظّٰىۚ‏(14)\nFA-ANZARTOKUM NAARAN TALAZZAA.\nTherefore do I warn you of a Fire blazing fiercely; \nلَا يَصْلٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الْاَشْقَىۙ‏(15)\nLAA YASLAAHAA ILLAL ASHQAL.\nNone shall reach it but those most unfortunate ones \nالَّذِىْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(16)\nLAZEE KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nWho give the lie to Truth and turn their backs. \nوَسَيُجَنَّبُهَا الْاَتْقَىۙ‏(17)\nWA SAYOJANNABOHAL ATQAL.\nBut those most devoted to Allah shall be removed far from it, \nالَّذِىْ يُؤْتِىْ مَالَهٗ يَتَزَكّٰىۚ‏(18)\nLAZEE YOATEE MAALAHU UATAZAKKAA.\nThose who spend their wealth for increase in self-purification, \nوَمَا لِاَحَدٍ عِنْدَهٗ مِنْ نِّعْمَةٍ تُجْزٰٓىۙ‏(19)\nWA MAA LE-AHADIN I’NDAHU MIN NEA’MATIN TUJZAA.\nAnd have in their minds no favour from anyone for which a reward is expected in return, \nاِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْاَعْلٰىۚ‏(20)\nILLAAB TEGHAAA-A WAJHE RABBEHIL A-A’LAA.\nBut only the desire to seek for the Countenance of their Lord Most High; \nوَلَسَوْفَ يَرْضٰى‏(21)\nWA LASAWFA YARZAA.\nAnd soon will they attain (complete) satisfaction. "
